  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Calculate the number of terms in the following arithmetic series. \n\n$$\n5.5+6+6.5+...=77.5\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series:\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\n$$\n\nWe have been given the sum ${S}_{N}=77.5,$ and the first term ${a}_{1}=5.5.$ Our goal is to find $N,$ the number of terms.\n\nThe common difference $d$ can be found, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{2}-{a}_{1} \\\\  & =6-5.5 \\\\  & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 77.5 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2(5.5)+(N-1)(0.5)) \\\\ 155 & =N(11+0.5N-0.5) \\\\ 155 & =N(10.5+0.5N) \\\\ 155 & =10.5N+0.5{N}^{2} \\\\ 0.5{N}^{2}+10.5N-155 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the equation above, the quadratic formula gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N & =\\frac{-10.5\\pm \\sqrt{(-10.5)^{2}-4\\cdot 0.5\\cdot (-155)}}{2\\cdot 0.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{-10.5\\pm 20.5}{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $N=10$ or $N=-31.$ We disregard the negative solution since $N$ must be positive.\n\nTherefore, our series has $N=10$ terms.",
